![Vector diagram](images/26/261d12a56adceb39a06d29e0a39abc6e839909025587c60989d0903bc04d7e9b.png)

Given that $\mathbf{c}=\lambda\mathbf{a}+\mu\mathbf{b}$, find $\lambda$ and $\mu$.

$\lambda=$ {{field-1}}

$\mu=$ {{field-2}}"] [:db/add "4fac9158-dfdb-5b87-889d-9cccc9068bbb" :question/worked-solution "![Completed vector route](images/37/37cde014f9c3a9e3a654530709ac908b001cdd887709ebb96a957ffe0968f92b.png)

Construct the route $O\to X\to C$, first parallel to $\mathbf{a}$ and then parallel to $\mathbf{b}$.

Along $OX$, move $3$ squares left. A copy of $\mathbf{a}$ moves $1$ square left. Thus $OX=3|\mathbf{a}|$ and the segment points in the same direction to $\mathbf{a}$. Hence $\overrightarrow{OX}=3\mathbf{a}$.

Along $XC$, move $1$ square left and $2$ squares down. A copy of $\mathbf{b}$ moves $1$ square left and $2$ squares down. Thus $XC=1|\mathbf{b}|$ and the segment points in the same direction to $\mathbf{b}$. Hence $\overrightarrow{XC}=\mathbf{b}$.

$$
\begin{aligned}
\mathbf{c}&=\overrightarrow{OX}+\overrightarrow{XC}\\&=3\mathbf{a}+\mathbf{b}
\end{aligned}
$$

Since $\mathbf{a}$ and $\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, their coefficients are unique. Matching coefficients gives $\lambda=3$ and $\mu=1$."] [:db/add "4fac9158-dfdb-5b87-889d-9cccc9068bbb" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [:db/add "4fac9158-dfdb-5b87-889d-9cccc9068bbb" :question/answer-fields "5245cf53-eec4-5f4b-8d6b-7cf7fd927606"] [:db/add "4fac9158-dfdb-5b87-889d-9cccc9068bbb" :question/answer-fields "ba3691cf-1ef0-54cd-ada6-23c1a5d67bfb"] [:db/ensure "4fac9158-dfdb-5b87-889d-9cccc9068bbb" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186096652 :knowledge-point/questions "4fac9158-dfdb-5b87-889d-9cccc9068bbb"] [:db/add "90c91475-590b-5e00-8285-6299a5d31cda" :answer/id #uuid "90c91475-590b-5e00-8285-6299a5d31cda"] [:db/add "90c91475-590b-5e00-8285-6299a5d31cda" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "90c91475-590b-5e00-8285-6299a5d31cda" :answer/value "2"] [:db/ensure "90c91475-590b-5e00-8285-6299a5d31cda" :answer/validate] [:db/add "666898ba-bbe5-5cf0-be09-0c9e47ed24ca" :answer-field/id #uuid "666898ba-bbe5-5cf0-be09-0c9e47ed24ca"] [:db/add "666898ba-bbe5-5cf0-be09-0c9e47ed24ca" :answer-field/key "field-1"] [:db/add "666898ba-bbe5-5cf0-be09-0c9e47ed24ca" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "666898ba-bbe5-5cf0-be09-0c9e47ed24ca" :answer-field/choices "90c91475-590b-5e00-8285-6299a5d31cda"] [:db/add "666898ba-bbe5-5cf0-be09-0c9e47ed24ca" :answer-field/correct "90c91475-590b-5e00-8285-6299a5d31cda"] [:db/ensure "666898ba-bbe5-5cf0-be09-0c9e47ed24ca" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "5f98edeb-91ab-5314-aac5-6f201d6c28a7" :answer/id #uuid "5f98edeb-91ab-5314-aac5-6f201d6c28a7"] [:db/add "5f98edeb-91ab-5314-aac5-6f201d6c28a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "5f98edeb-91ab-5314-aac5-6f201d6c28a7" :answer/value "4"] [:db/ensure "5f98edeb-91ab-5314-aac5-6f201d6c28a7" :answer/validate] [:db/add "d3a941ed-e775-596b-870f-23d6b124cb3b" :answer-field/id #uuid "d3a941ed-e775-596b-870f-23d6b124cb3b"] [:db/add "d3a941ed-e775-596b-870f-23d6b124cb3b" :answer-field/key "field-2"] [:db/add "d3a941ed-e775-596b-870f-23d6b124cb3b" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "d3a941ed-e775-596b-870f-23d6b124cb3b" :answer-field/choices "5f98edeb-91ab-5314-aac5-6f201d6c28a7"] [:db/add "d3a941ed-e775-596b-870f-23d6b124cb3b" :answer-field/correct "5f98edeb-91ab-5314-aac5-6f201d6c28a7"] [:db/ensure "d3a941ed-e775-596b-870f-23d6b124cb3b" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "10155d1b-0d1c-5dfa-a752-9c65ac5d600c" :question/id #uuid "10155d1b-0d1c-5dfa-a752-9c65ac5d600c"] [:db/add "10155d1b-0d1c-5dfa-a752-9c65ac5d600c" :question/problem "The vectors are drawn on a square grid: $\overrightarrow{OA}=\mathbf{a}$, $\overrightarrow{OB}=\mathbf{b}$, and $\overrightarrow{OC}=\mathbf{c}$.

![Vector diagram](images/00/0017e5d7fc8701f0a038ef80a8c8bce552f568dd5708aae29b28e050e74d3591.png)

Given that $\mathbf{c}=\lambda\mathbf{a}+\mu\mathbf{b}$, find $\lambda$ and $\mu$.

$\lambda=$ {{field-1}}

$\mu=$ {{field-2}}"] [:db/add "10155d1b-0d1c-5dfa-a752-9c65ac5d600c" :question/worked-solution "![Completed vector route](images/a6/a6a7400a3b0aafed09994ce692174418fae00d0e56aade003e7ac77d7c922ca1.png)

Construct the route $O\to X\to C$, first parallel to $\mathbf{b}$ and then parallel to $\mathbf{a}$.

Along $OX$, move $8$ squares up. A copy of $\mathbf{b}$ moves $2$ squares up. Thus $OX=4|\mathbf{b}|$ and the segment points in the same direction to $\mathbf{b}$. Hence $\overrightarrow{OX}=4\mathbf{b}$.

Along $XC$, move $2$ squares left and $2$ squares up. A copy of $\mathbf{a}$ moves $1$ square left and $1$ square up. Thus $XC=2|\mathbf{a}|$ and the segment points in the same direction to $\mathbf{a}$. Hence $\overrightarrow{XC}=2\mathbf{a}$.

$$
\begin{aligned}
\mathbf{c}&=\overrightarrow{OX}+\overrightarrow{XC}\\&=4\mathbf{b}+2\mathbf{a}\\&=2\mathbf{a}+4\mathbf{b}
\end{aligned}
$$

